ProsperoSunshine: sunshine.conf sets the error correction for clients over the internet apart

fec_percentage is one number for every client: the share of Reed-Solomon packets added to the video, which rtsp.cpp takes
out of the bitrate the client asked for. A wired client at home loses next to nothing and would rather have the bitrate;
a phone on mobile data loses more. internet_fec_percentage (0 to 100, unset by default) is the share for a client over
the internet, which is one that asks for Moonlight's small packets (prospero::remote_packet_size, as the pacing of patch
0026 has it); unset, or out of range, such a client gets fec_percentage as before. Both places that use the share ask
prospero::fec_share (video/frame_pacing.hpp): the encoder's bitrate in rtsp.cpp and the shards in stream.cpp.

